{
  "name": "Investigating environmental crimes in East Africa",
  "parent_id": 203313841790202,
  "group_id": "b3dea95b-f4b6-4f2d-93b0-7aa03ce13a7a",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:29:13.122Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-31T09:29:13.198Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-31T09:29:13.186Z",
  "id": 203983065622110,
  "uuid": "102b7e1e-7af9-4ff2-b9f8-2b1b7d174fab",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "9accadd6-29c6-7ff4-633d-4fa9d3b2f088",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "9d4f22ee-6265-32a6-bf49-407112b7a5dc",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"I didn't pay much attention to environmental stories because most newsrooms I worked for are more into current affairs and human-interest stories that require the least effort,\" she said. \"The status quo in Kenyan newsrooms is dictated by media ownership which decides what takes precedence in the news. Environmental stories are hardly given priority.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "There is also a fear that science or environmental stories are too technical and expensive to cover. But Faith is a member of DIRAJ, the Disaster Risk Reduction Association of Journalists, which trains journalists to report on climate change and disaster risk reduction. Coupled with the new grant, she has developed a confidence and interest in reporting on environmental issues. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Through her investigative reporting, Faith has found that rising water levels and variation in rainfall patterns are key environmental concerns in the region. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"These two issues have had a direct impact on livelihoods, food security and health. They are also leading to conflict, as we are witnessing in pastoral regions like Laikipia in northern Kenya, where grazing lands are becoming degraded as seasonal rains fall short. This forces communities to invade private crop lands that are also struggling due to extreme rain variations.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Journalists have a role to educate, inform and entertain the public. Faith believes the same applies to environmental sustainability, with media playing a vital role in raising awareness amongst people. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"There is need for journalists to create a culture of producing and consuming environment stories, especially now that social media has revolutionized the industry. We need to be creative and entertaining so that the reporting is consumed by younger audiences. I look forward to the day when newsrooms will put environmental news at par with politics.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Media across the world has seen a huge rise in female journalists. They are winning awards and crossing boundaries that were seen as male-dominated such as investigative journalism. Faith sees this as progressive but believes training in environmental reporting can change the game. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Women of this generation are capable of working on stories around anything. However, we need more upskilling opportunities. We should not ignore the fact that women journalists in some cultures are still facing discrimination and sexism. It is important that we sensitize society that women's impact and contributions can be felt - we are not here to be seen, but to be heard.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "And on that note, is Faith practising what she preaches? ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Of course! I don't litter plastics. I ensure that I put my trash in a designated bin. I also love trees, an interest that I picked from my dad. Our rural home is quite forested with trees of different species. As a young girl, I would water and care for the trees my dad planted, and I still do the same to date. This has had an influence on where I live as an adult. Nature fascinates me!\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
